# NSG call/session dynamics — traffic that breathes instead of a constant faucet.
#
# Reference note (distro trees are the source of truth; build-slim.sh bakes
# them). The Tera5G-class "average call duration / time between calls" model,
# at the scale this engine can actually observe.
#
# ── Config (platform side) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ServiceRequirement gains two optional fields (schema.py):
#   avg_call_duration_s   mean length of an active burst (exponential)
#   avg_idle_duration_s   mean silence between bursts (exponential)
# Omit both = the classic continuous stream (fully backward compatible).
# The AI config-generator prompt teaches the fields (llm_agent.py).
#
# ── Spec string (backend -> engine) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Level-5 per-UE spec extends "qci,rate_mbps" -> "qci,rate_mbps[,on_s,off_s]".
# TIME COMPRESSION (_ue_slice_specs, main.py): the mmWave sim only advances
# ~1-2 SIMULATED seconds inside a run window, and ns-3's OnOffApplication
# starts with an Off period — so human-scale call times (30 s calls) would
# never toggle and traffic would read zero (observed). The backend therefore
# rescales the pair to a <= 1 s period with the EXACT on:off ratio preserved:
# what the RIC test needs from a call model is the load STRUCTURE (duty cycle
# + fluctuation), not the literal seconds. 2 s / 20 s -> 0.091 / 0.909.
#
# ── Scenario (scratch/scenario-zero-with_parallel_loging.cc) ─────────────────
# Slice parse now reads the optional 3rd/4th fields (old 2-field strings keep
# working). When a call model is present, DL and UL traffic use
# OnOffApplication (UDP, 1400 B, DataRate = slice rate / 25% for UL) with
# ExponentialRandomVariable On/Off times; otherwise the CBR UdpClient path is
# unchanged.
#
# ── VERIFIED on the real engine (2026-07-17) ─────────────────────────────────
# Same offered rate (20 Mbps/UE), continuous vs ~9% duty cycle:
#   continuous : DRB.UEThpDl mean 10.1 Mbps (per-UE 6.9-14.4)
#   bursty     : mean 4.8 Mbps, per-UE spread 0.0 -> 16.4 Mbps
# i.e. some report windows silent, some in full burst — the load fluctuation
# a RIC test needs. Engine test: engines/nsoran/test_calls.py; unit test of
# the compression in the harness path; fidelity lever "L5 call dynamics"
# rides the full config -> backend -> engine path.
#
# ── KNOWN OPEN (tracked) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The KPM reporting path can sample ZERO-counter windows (PRB/UL zero while
# throughput flows): deterministic under buildings, intermittent on the plain
# baseline. Guarded red by fidelity "L4 PRB consistency"; root-cause task
# spawned (counter reset/window race or stale rnti/cell keys).
